Patch: pangolin-5cf94b8-mask-per-gene-1
Upstream: https://github.com/tkzeng/Pangolin
Applies to: 5cf94b8db938c658391b4305cd7ce33297d44ff7 (main as of 2026-09-24)
Upstream pangolin/pangolin.py SHA-256: f3f25c4febf64d01ef42f967dc5cf10f6856bf3aa92d26f09803ad408169da9b
Patched pangolin/pangolin.py SHA-256: see mfass.pangolin_patch.PATCHED_SOURCE_SHA256
Installed version identity: 1.0.2+rewire.maskpergene1

process_variant masks the per-strand loss/gain arrays in place inside the
per-gene loop, so masking for one gene alters the scores reported for every
later gene on the same strand (upstream issue #29). This patch gives each gene
its own copy of the strand arrays. With mask=False the arrays are never
modified, so output is unchanged. Equivalent to unmerged upstream PR #30,
which its author closed on 2025-07-16 without upstream review.

Licence: this is a modification of Pangolin, which is GPL-3.0. The patch and
any patched copy of Pangolin are distributed under GPL-3.0, not this
repository's licence. Apply with: git apply <this file> in a clean checkout
of the revision above.

diff --git a/pangolin/pangolin.py b/pangolin/pangolin.py
index 194736f..a3dc91d
--- a/pangolin/pangolin.py
+++ b/pangolin/pangolin.py
@@ -130,11 +130,14 @@ def process_variant(lnum, chr, pos, ref, alt, gtf, models, args):
         loss_neg, gain_neg = compute_score(ref_seq, alt_seq, '-', d, models)
 
     scores_list = []
-    for (genes, loss, gain) in (
+    for (genes, strand_loss, strand_gain) in (
         (genes_pos,loss_pos,gain_pos),(genes_neg,loss_neg,gain_neg)
     ):
         # Emit a bundle of scores/warnings per gene; join them all later
         for gene, positions in genes.items():
+            # rewire mask-per-gene patch: masking below edits these arrays in
+            # place, so each gene gets its own copy of the strand's scores.
+            loss, gain = strand_loss.copy(), strand_gain.copy()
             per_gene_scores = []
             warnings = "Warnings:"
             positions = np.array(positions)
